<title>UK: NWE gasoline steady despite futures rise, arb shut.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline steady despite futures rise, arb shut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE gasoline prices were steady on Tuesday despite firmer futures amid slack demand for product, traders said.</p>
<p>Eurograde barges were heard to have traded at $192 a tonne fob ARA and the arbitrage window was still considered notionally closed, although dealers said they were unwilling to make firm assessments of the trans-Atlantic arbitrage window before the open of U.S. markets.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
